{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvamL1PFMa51SugBSEN8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Don't approve the six-week study as proposed. Reshape it into a small, time-boxed, conditional step.**\n\n**Why:** The bank has given no timeline or volume, and no other customer has asked for on-premise. Six weeks of an engineer is a real cost, and the study would answer a question the bank hasn't committed to. Also, \"feasible\" isn't the real question. Supporting on-premise means ongoing costs for packaging, upgrades, support, and security reviews. A study won't show those costs, and once you start, the commitment tends to stick.\n\n**What I'd do:**\n\n1. **Find out what the requirement really is.** Legal teams often write on-premise as a default template. Ask whether the real concerns are data residency, control of keys, or network isolation. A single-tenant deployment in a private VPC, or in the bank's own cloud account, may satisfy it at a fraction of the cost.\n2. **Cap the technical work at about one week.** Have an engineer do a desk review covering architecture, external dependencies, and the biggest blockers. The output should be a rough effort range and a list of deal-breakers, with no prototype.\n3. **Tie further investment to something from the bank.** Examples are a paid pilot, a signed letter of intent with a volume floor, or a named executive sponsor. If they won't commit to any of these, park the on-premise work and say so politely.\n4. **Keep the rest of the deal moving.** Offer the non-on-premise parts now, so the four months of negotiation aren't wasted.\n\n**Decision rule:** If the one-week review finds a cheap path (for example, a customer-managed cloud deployment) and the bank commits to something, go ahead. If not, park it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3451,"cache_read_input_tokens":5000,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3451},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a225779d-4f92-48fa-89ee-bc14e1314afe","uuid":"33d2deb3-5fa4-4926-be72-217fcc2b25cc","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:09:49.073Z","request_id":"req_011CfvamKm1LLSHyPXFX7A7z"}
